sentences.text:
1. The petitioner through the instant petition filed as Public Interest Litigation has, inter-alia, sought following directions :-
a) Issue a writ in the nature of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or direction under Article 226 of the Constitution of India, directing the respondents to prevent entry of camels within their jurisdictional area;
b) Issue a writ in the nature of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or direction under Article 226 of the Constitution of India, directing respondent No.3 to ensure that no camels are being illegally transported into Haryana and in the event, that they are then, to immediately cease the animals and give their custody to a nearby Gaushala who will then bear the responsibility of transporting the animals back to Rajasthan or Gujarat and give them to an NGO there;

